The automatic graphics card (app/Sources/LullabySettings: GPUIdentity in GameConfig,
ConfigMaterializer's GPU lines and dxvk.conf) follows Sevoflurane's Core/GPUIdentity.swift
and Core/GPUEquivalence.swift: which cards stand in for an Apple chip, their PCI ids, the
driver version strings and the variables each renderer reads. Same MIT license as above,
Copyright (c) 2026 kageroumado.

steam/hook/hooks/hook_launch.c, np_rebind_import in steam/hook/core/macho.c, steam/hook/tests/launch-shell.c
and the LaunchBuilder::SteamVRSupportCheck signature come from upstream NotProton 1.1.0
(https://github.com/NotProtonNot/NotProton, GPL-3.0, the project this one is a fork of),
written there by NotProtonNot with Logan (LaganYT); NotProton's own change records the
names in NOTPROTON_ENV_BASE.

Dormison, the engine NotProton runs games on, is Wine with wine-staging and its own
changes, LGPL-2.1-or-later (https://github.com/kageroumado/dormison). NotProton downloads
it from Dormison's own signed releases. NotProton rebuilds single files of it from the
same commit and puts them in place, the release's file kept beside each: the ntdll.dll
loader hook (docs/DECISIONS.md P3-1) and the fixes in patches/engine/patches (A0910-9 and
later). Each rebuilt file is first proven equal to the release's, instruction for
instruction, without the patches. These files stay LGPL-2.1-or-later; their sources are
Dormison's commit plus the patches in this repository.

Dormison's release carries, unchanged, DXMT (Direct3D 10/11 on Metal, Feifan He for
CodeWeavers, LGPL-2.1-or-later), DXVK (Philip Rebohle, zlib) and MoltenVK (The Brenwill
Workshop and The Khronos Group, Apache-2.0); each keeps the license it ships with.

Two of those engine fixes are Highball's (https://github.com/gauthierpiarrette/highball-engine,
patches to Wine, LGPL-2.1-or-later): 0018 (commit charge is the footprint) and 0020 (Retina
HORZRES, itself from athei/wine fa43d6db2). Their headers name the source.

Raw mouse input through GameController (patches/engine/patches/winemac.so/0004, lby-octavia-gcmouse) is
Elvin Hayatov's Wine merge request !11799 (Copyright 2026 Elvin Hayatov, LGPL-2.1-or-later),
taken from WineForge 0.6.0.7 (https://github.com/Alien4042x/WineForge, commit 8051e02d). Lullaby's
changes to it: GameController is loaded at run time instead of linked (no Makefile.in edit), the
trackpad is left to the system, and the speed follows the mouse's resolution or the
LULLABY_GCMOUSE_SCALE launch option.

The mouse look patch (ENG-16, patches/engine/patches/winemac.so/0007-winemac-mouse-look-pointer-lock.patch:
the pointer detached from the mouse while a game hides the cursor, so it never reaches the Dock or the menu bar)
is adapted from kit/patches/wine-winemac-mouselook.patch of Black Ops Mac (https://github.com/sirdankdabs/bo-mac,
MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2026 Black Ops Mac contributors), ported by hand to Dormison r7 and Lullaby's series.
The MIT permission notice of that project applies to the idea and the parts taken; the patch as built into
winemac.so is LGPL-2.1-or-later like Wine. Lullaby's changes: only the game's own recentring SetCursorPos is
ignored, GetCursorPos keeps Wine's own position during the look, the system cursor is hidden for the look,
LULLABY_MOUSELOOK=0 turns it off.

The run script's routing by verb (EA, Ubisoft and other launchers), the Steam Input
controller handling, the batched prefix registry import, steam.exe's std handles and
Ubisoft Connect's install path values come from upstream NotProton 1.1.x (GPL-3.0),
adapted to Dormison.

mtld3d (Direct3D 9 on Metal, https://github.com/athei/mtld3d, zlib licence, by athei) and WineMetalGL
(OpenGL on Metal, https://github.com/metalsharp/WineMetalGL, LGPL-3.0-or-later, by MetalSharp) are not
part of this repository and are not built by it: when a game needs one, Lullaby downloads the author's
release (the exact versions and sha256 are pinned in the run script and in release/components.json)
and checks the hash before it uses the files.

D3DMetal is Apple's, from the Game Porting Toolkit each player downloads from Apple and
adds; NotProton neither ships nor downloads it.

Lullaby's nvapi64.dll (patches/inject/lby-rainbowdash-reflex/) stands in front of D3DMetal's and answers NVIDIA
Reflex. Its function names come from NVIDIA's nvapi_interface.h and its structures from
nvapi.h (https://github.com/NVIDIA/nvapi, MIT, Copyright (c) 2024 NVIDIA CORPORATION &
AFFILIATES). The idea of holding a frame back in the game's Sleep so that none waits in a
queue comes from Korthos Software's low_latency_layer
(https://github.com/Korthos-Software/low_latency_layer, MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 Korthos
Software Pty Ltd); the pacing itself (release by when the screen shows frames) is Lullaby's
own, and no code is taken.

From upstream NotProton 1.2.0 (GPL-3.0, the same licence as this repository) Lullaby took, written again for its own tree: no std handles for a program that gets a console of its own (bridge/steam-shim/steam.cpp), the microphone, camera and local network usage keys and `caffeinate` in the launcher bundle, and the `Steam.dll` link for Prey with its removal in Uninstall (steam/hook/feats/compat_run.sh, app/Sources/LullabyApp/Model/Uninstall.swift).
